reviewerChecks:
Criterion 3: five separate cases, each with its own installation, each asserting status 'refused', its reason and zero executor calls: not_authorized, expired (triggered after expiresOn, not an already-expired install), mode_mismatch, focus_unknown (the proposal has skipDuringFocus:true and focusActive is null), and invalid_state or state_or_adapter_unavailable for a changed installer-written record. Superficially passing but wrong:
- the focus case without skipDuringFocus;
- an expired case that only asserts the installer throws;
- a refusal that is really 'duplicate_or_old_trigger' because the installation was reused;
- 'changed installation' done by writing a brand-new record rather than editing the installer's output.

Criterion 4: the effect-then-fail case uses failureBehavior 'retry_once', and its run writes an effect under the temp root and then throws. It asserts 'outcome_unknown', one launch and one effect line; a later call gives 'stopped' with no new launch. The pending case uses a real child process exit (assert.rejects with code 73). It asserts ledger phase 'pending', a restart refused 'busy_or_unavailable', lock removal only after the child exited, then 'outcome_unknown' with no launches. Superficially passing but wrong:
- a run that returns {ok:false} (never 'launched' semantics);
- failureBehavior 'stop' only;
- the ledger hand-edited to 'pending';
- restart asserted only as 'not succeeded'.
